From df23ad7f955bc7c3c4291bfb097385bad8fb5445 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Windows fixes <noreply@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:41:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: path handling in the read-only guard and the panel,
 test portability

- skills/map/SKILL.md: quote the description; its unquoted ": " made the
  frontmatter invalid YAML, so the skill loaded with no metadata.
- hooks/contesto.ts: barre(), relativoA(), percorsoDentro() handle C:\ paths
  (backslashes are separators, drive letter and case ignored) only on Windows;
  POSIX paths are unchanged. eSegreto() splits on / and \ so C:\repo\.env
  stays a secret.
- hooks/register.tsx: the mappa-role write guard and leggiScelti() use those
  helpers. On Windows the guard denied every write to docs/mappa/ and the
  panel read 0 files, because git gives C:/... and the engine C:\....
- tests: fs mock compares paths in test form; new unit test for Windows paths;
  test_struttura.py decodes output as UTF-8 and removes read-only git objects.
- scripts/struttura.py: stderr in UTF-8 too; git output decoded as UTF-8.
- docs/DECISIONI.md: one line for the Windows-only normalisation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
